One common way to introduce vulnerabilities is through **Insecure Deserialization**. When an application uses `ObjectInputStream` to deserialize untrusted data from a user, an attacker can craft a malicious serialized object to execute arbitrary code on the server.

```java
import java.io.*;

public class DeserializationExample {
    // This method is vulnerable because it accepts an InputStream from an untrusted source
    public Object deserializeData(InputStream inputStream) throws IOException, ClassNotFoundException {
        // The use of ObjectInputStream on untrusted input is a major security risk
        ObjectInputStream ois = new ObjectInputStream(inputStream);
        // Deserializing data here can lead to Remote Code Execution (RCE)
        return ois.readObject();
    }
}
